{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>My wrong is upon you.</b> The wrong done to me — I lay the punishment upon you. When you prayed to the Holy One, blessed be He, 'What will You give me, for I go childless' — you prayed only for yourself; you should have prayed for both of us, and I too would have been remembered along with you. And still more: your words — you do me violence with them, for you hear my humiliation and are silent (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>I gave my handmaid, etc., between me and between you.</b> Every בֵּינֶיךָ in Scripture is deficient (without a yod), but this one is full — read it בֵינַיִךְ, 'between me and my children': she cast the evil eye upon Hagar's pregnancy and caused her to miscarry. That the angel says to Hagar, 'Behold, you are pregnant' — but she had already conceived; is he announcing to her that she will conceive? Rather, it teaches that she lost the first pregnancy."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:57.809336857Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}